  "body": "`internal/gui/tests/proto-menu-overflow.test.cjs` \"chromium en: a quota picker taller than the window clamps and scrolls\" went red once in a whole GUI suite run (`node --test --test-concurrency=3 internal/gui/tests/*.test.cjs`, feedback-1022 at e352cc823 on origin/main 7dd965ed2, load ~35-45 with other sessions' suites):\n\n```\n✖ chromium en: a quota picker taller than the window clamps and scrolls (1843.315375ms)\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: the last account was picked and saved: undefined\n      at TestContext.<anonymous> (internal/gui/tests/proto-menu-overflow.test.cjs:110:14)\n```\n\nAlone it passes 4 of 4, on main 7dd965ed2 and on the branch.\n\nCause, by reading the test: after `last.click()` and Escape it reads `posts.at(-1)` straight away (line 109). The save is an async POST that the route handler records, and nothing waits for it, so a busy machine reads the list before the POST arrives. Fix: wait for the POST (`page.waitForRequest` set up before the click, or poll `posts` for trayUsages), not the click's return.\n\nNot taking it.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
