   "body": "Implemented in the fork: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/quota-picker-save-test\n\nThe test now waits until the settings handler has recorded the save before reading `trayUsages`. The fixture deliberately holds recording until after the click and Escape have returned, then releases it explicitly. Removing the await deterministically gives the reported `undefined`; no fixed delay or loaded machine is needed. The assertion now checks the exact last account, rather than accepting any account from the list.\n\nBoth Chromium and WebKit pass all five languages (10 cases) in Playwright 1.62.1. With the await removed, both engines fail the last-account assertion. Browser fixtures run without network access.\n\nCombined verification at https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/c61bf9b7315a12ccde15e0b6ef393f5e51771019: Go 1.26.8, umask 027, isolated HOME with caches pinned; native/Linux nogui/Windows vet and builds passed, and `go test -tags nogui ./... -count=1 -timeout=45m` passed (69 packages passed, 19 have no tests). Windows validation is cross-vet/build; native Windows/macOS runtimes were not exercised.\n\nThis corrects the test's synchronization; the production quota-picker behavior is unchanged.\n",
