   "body": "That second sighting is the same race as the first: the chromium zh case at the same `proto-menu-overflow.test.cjs:110` assertion, on a loaded machine — the picker's save POST lands after `last.click()` and Escape have returned, and the test reads `posts` before the route handler records it. Alone it passes because the POST usually wins the race.\n\nThe branch above is current again: `fix/quota-picker-save-test` now sits on today's main (be7f1746) as the single test commit [066a4cab](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/066a4cab) (it was previously based on an older batch; the earlier combined verification c61bf9b7 stays reachable via `fix/issue-batch-20261023-e`). The fixture holds the settings route's recording until after the click has returned, then releases it, and the test awaits the recorded save — so the order no longer depends on machine load.\n\nVerified at that head, no network: all ten cases pass (Chromium and WebKit × en, zh, zh-TW, ja, de; Playwright 1.60.0 here vs 1.62.1 on the pinned Noble image before). Negative control: removing the single `await saved` makes all ten fail the last-account assertion deterministically on an idle machine — the reported `undefined` without needing load.",
